# No AI typography artifacts

Do **not** use smart / AI-flavored punctuation in product UI copy, i18n strings, commit messages, PR text, rules, or other agent-authored prose.

## Forbidden

| Avoid | Use instead |
| --- | --- |
| Em dash (U+2014) | ASCII hyphen-minus `-`, comma, colon, or a new sentence |
| En dash (U+2013) | ASCII `-` (including ranges: `1-25`, `18-28`) |
| Curly double quotes (U+201C / U+201D) | Straight `"..."` |
| Curly single quotes used as quotes (U+2018 / U+2019) | Straight `"..."` or ASCII apostrophe `'` |
| Guillemets (U+00AB / U+00BB) | Straight `"..."` |

Also avoid other LLM copy tells in UI strings: the ellipsis character (U+2026) when `...` is enough, decorative non-breaking spaces, and middle dots in sentences unless the surrounding UI already uses that pattern.

## Allowed exception (product glyph only)

A single em dash may appear **only** as the dedicated missing-value glyph behind the i18n key `format.emDash` (or an equivalent single-purpose key). Do not paste that character into surrounding sentence prose; explain it in words ("em dash glyph") or interpolate that key.

## When editing existing copy

Replace forbidden characters in any string you touch. Prefer fixing whole i18n keys you change, not leaving mixed styles in the same sentence.
